		c	Convenience method to construct a Slice from a readable literal. Not intended for data parsing - no validation is performed and various errors can be thrown by this method for malformed data. ,<p>, The format is simple; every pair of characters is interpreted as a hex byte, and any chars between square brackets ([ and ]) have their lower 8 bits passed through as-is. For example:,<br/>, ,<code>,89[PNG\r\n]1A[\n],</code>,<br/>, will become,<br/>, ,<code>,89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A | .PNG....,</code>
